11:49.020 --> 11:52.020
<b>Starting Life
 in Another 
World With 
My Big Sister</b>

12:04.490 --> 12:05.870
Where am I?

12:06.580 --> 12:08.050
You're awake, Asahi?

12:08.740 --> 12:10.030
Maya-nee...

12:14.350 --> 12:17.790
I'm so glad. If you didn't wake up, I...

12:17.790 --> 12:21.010
It's all right. I just swallowed 
a bit of water, that's all.

12:21.240 --> 12:24.870
Even if the worst happened and you were 
transported to another world again,

12:25.350 --> 12:27.890
your big sister would follow you there.

12:28.430 --> 12:30.140
Yeah. Thanks.

12:31.530 --> 12:34.020
More importantly, where are we?
 Where are the others?

12:34.020 --> 12:36.260
About that... I'm sorry.

12:36.260 --> 12:39.900
I was so desperate to save you, 
I ended up getting swept away, too.

12:40.360 --> 12:41.900
Then, this is...

12:42.140 --> 12:48.000
While you were out, I took a look around, 
but the island seems uninhabited.

12:48.000 --> 12:49.410
What?

12:49.770 --> 12:54.920
I'm sure Kilmaria or whoever will eventually 
sense our presence and come find us.

12:55.320 --> 12:56.940
I guess you're right.

12:56.940 --> 13:00.730
So it's a life of adventure on the
deserted island we drifted up on, huh?

13:00.730 --> 13:02.920
Sounds like fun, in its own way.

13:02.920 --> 13:03.920
Hup.

13:03.920 --> 13:06.780
Are you all right? 
Shouldn't you rest a little more?

13:06.780 --> 13:08.160
I'm fine, I'm fine.

13:08.160 --> 13:11.390
It's more important that I get a
 bunch of stuff ready before dark.

13:13.140 --> 13:15.890
All right. Just don't push yourself too hard.

13:16.240 --> 13:20.900
I won't. First, we need to secure food
 and water. Then, somewhere to sleep.

13:21.260 --> 13:24.370
This kinda reminds me of our 
family camping trip a long time ago.

13:24.370 --> 13:28.610
Oh, yes. Back when you were small
 and cute and had such soft skin.

13:28.610 --> 13:31.310
Of course, you're still cute now, Asahi.

13:31.310 --> 13:32.910
You seriously never change.

13:34.870 --> 13:36.910
Well, let's head out!

14:31.310 --> 14:33.050
All right!

14:31.870 --> 14:33.050
<b>Stone-Throwing Skill Has Leveled Up!</b>

14:33.050 --> 14:35.060
<b>Maya</b>

14:33.050 --> 14:35.060
<b>Asahi</b>

14:46.400 --> 14:49.990
<b>Maya</b>

14:46.400 --> 14:49.990
<b>Asahi</b>

14:51.450 --> 14:54.250
That fish was tastier than I thought it'd be.

14:54.250 --> 14:56.060
So was that bird you brought down.

14:56.060 --> 14:58.520
Maybe it's thanks to your cooking skills.

14:58.880 --> 15:01.840
Well, I know your tastes 
inside and out, Asahi.

15:03.520 --> 15:05.090
You know, lately...

15:05.090 --> 15:09.000
With the Super Asahi Legion and everything, 
things have gotten crazy lively,

15:09.000 --> 15:13.800
but when we first came to this world, 
it was just the two of us, right?

15:15.420 --> 15:18.980
I always pray it'll be 
just the two of us, Asahi.

15:19.660 --> 15:24.980
But it's not like you hate hanging out with Kilmaria
and everyone in the Super Asahi Legion, right?

15:27.290 --> 15:30.860
Hey, Maya-nee. How do you feel 
after coming to this world?

15:30.860 --> 15:32.410
I...

15:32.800 --> 15:34.480
I'm happy every single day.

15:35.410 --> 15:38.370
Because I get to see you every day.

15:38.950 --> 15:40.010
And...

15:42.280 --> 15:44.130
Because you seem to be having fun.

15:44.570 --> 15:45.930
Maya-nee...

15:46.570 --> 15:47.800
I guess that's true.

15:51.970 --> 15:56.750
To be honest, in the beginning, I was a 
little scared and didn't know what to do.

15:56.750 --> 15:59.030
But because you were always there for me...

16:00.060 --> 16:04.050
I think usually when something like this 
happens, it's normal to feel more hopeless.

16:04.730 --> 16:07.900
After all, I didn't have a cheat skill 
like you see in lots of stories.

16:08.120 --> 16:10.690
Actually, it's a really terrible situation.

16:10.690 --> 16:15.660
Like, I should've gotten <i>something</i>, you know?
A skill that made me OP or whatever.

16:16.330 --> 16:22.010
So... Normally, I'm too shy and 
embarrassed to say this, but...

16:23.910 --> 16:25.760
Thank you, Maya-nee.

16:30.410 --> 16:31.670
Asahi...

16:32.290 --> 16:34.400
And since that's the way things are,

16:34.400 --> 16:37.280
I'm sure there's still lots 
of fun stuff awaiting us.

16:37.280 --> 16:39.810
There'll likely be lots 
of difficult stuff, too,

16:39.810 --> 16:42.680
but with everyone's help, 
we'll find a way to handle those.

16:43.850 --> 16:45.600
Yeah. I'm sure you're right.

16:48.010 --> 16:50.530
I might've gotten a little chilled.

16:51.070 --> 16:52.900
I see. You're getting cold?

16:55.600 --> 16:59.160
In that case, come sleep with your sister! 
We can keep each other warm!

16:59.160 --> 17:01.560
And we're back to the same old pattern?

17:01.560 --> 17:06.330
Why are you so shy? You used to cry about 
being scared of ghosts and crawl into my bed.

17:06.330 --> 17:09.520
Do you even realize how long ago that was?!

17:12.220 --> 17:17.180
Are you the lowly humans 
who dared to defy the Sea King?

17:17.180 --> 17:19.100
We still had the boss left?

17:19.410 --> 17:22.320
I am the Great King Shark.

17:22.320 --> 17:25.060
I command this sea and the Ten Greatest.

17:25.360 --> 17:28.140
Persistent oil stains are enough
 persistence for us, thanks.

17:28.140 --> 17:29.900
We'll take care of you quickly and—

17:32.170 --> 17:33.610
It can't be!

17:35.020 --> 17:37.850
Elegant Split Buster!

17:38.330 --> 17:39.570
Disheveled Moonlight Blossom.

17:41.280 --> 17:43.040
Gloria! Kuon!

17:43.870 --> 17:45.040
Protection!

17:47.030 --> 17:48.210
How'd you all get here?

17:48.210 --> 17:51.210
We cannot simply leave you to it
when you two are in a pinch.

17:51.710 --> 17:53.070
This isn't a pinch!

17:53.070 --> 17:56.800
We decided we'd each get a day 
with Asahi on a deserted island, right?

17:56.800 --> 17:59.300
Huh? That sounds like 
some kind of variety show.

17:59.300 --> 18:03.430
I won Asahi Scramble, so I got the voucher!
Don't come out when you feel like it!

18:03.980 --> 18:08.190
Wait, does that mean everything 
Maya-nee and I said to each other...

18:08.620 --> 18:11.150
But because you were always there for me...

18:11.490 --> 18:12.610
Asahi...

18:12.840 --> 18:16.070
Normally, I'm too shy and 
embarrassed to say this, but...

18:16.440 --> 18:17.530
Asahi...

18:17.530 --> 18:18.860
Smooch.

18:19.380 --> 18:19.990
No!

18:19.990 --> 18:21.750
And we didn't go that far!

18:21.750 --> 18:22.780
No? How far then?

18:22.780 --> 18:24.200
Spill the beans!

18:24.200 --> 18:25.450
Huh? Um, well...

18:25.700 --> 18:27.850
Why are you so embarrassed?

18:27.850 --> 18:31.540
A brother and sister sharing their love
 for each other is totally natural!

18:33.690 --> 18:36.870
Look. A dangerous thing's 
attacking us, so let's focus on that!

18:39.420 --> 18:41.690
You dare to wrong us, foolish humans?

18:41.690 --> 18:43.500
You shall atone with your deaths!

18:43.500 --> 18:45.750
Assemble, champions of the sea!

18:45.750 --> 18:47.060
Right!

18:47.060 --> 18:48.390
They recovered?

19:26.460 --> 19:32.370
Super Great King Shark!

19:32.700 --> 19:33.990
Mark 2!

19:41.850 --> 19:44.200
This is my true form.

19:46.860 --> 19:48.780
Rendered speechless, I see.

19:48.780 --> 19:51.120
You shall perish in the depths of despair!

19:51.870 --> 19:54.830
Feel the power of the sea!

19:54.830 --> 19:57.340
This is bad! If that hits us...

19:58.100 --> 19:59.540
Honestly.

20:00.000 --> 20:01.860
Every single one of you...

20:10.970 --> 20:12.600
Big Sis Moses!

20:15.580 --> 20:16.730
What's going on?

20:17.090 --> 20:19.480
Th-That Maya is an absolute monster!

20:19.790 --> 20:24.030
You stole my precious time with Asahi.

20:24.030 --> 20:26.860
For that crime, you shall 
die a thousand deaths!

20:34.250 --> 20:37.460
Big Sis Omega Fire!

21:07.300 --> 21:09.530
Like I said, we weren't in a pinch.

21:09.530 --> 21:11.740
Then why didn't you take care of it sooner?

21:11.740 --> 21:14.370
Making it <i>look</i> like a tight spot,
 then saving him is cooler!

21:14.660 --> 21:18.440
That's Asahi's elder sister for you! 
I'll take note for future reference.

21:18.440 --> 21:20.390
Miss Maya is to be feared.

21:20.390 --> 21:21.340
Indeed.

21:23.480 --> 21:25.740
This whole thing is totally hopeless.

21:25.740 --> 21:28.390
But seems like everyone's having fun, right?

21:31.690 --> 21:34.030
Yeah. That's true.

23:09.120 --> 23:11.220
Doesn't look like it's stopping soon.

23:11.220 --> 23:15.280
Since my Stone-Throwing skill leveled up, 
I wanted to practice it, but...

23:16.410 --> 23:17.790
I'm so bored.

23:17.790 --> 23:20.300
That's because the beach was so much fun.

23:20.300 --> 23:21.290
In that case...

23:21.870 --> 23:23.210
Wanna play a game?

23:24.230 --> 23:27.210
Today's the day I show you my <i>true</i> abilities!

23:27.520 --> 23:31.370
You can play, but don't get too rowdy, okay?

23:31.370 --> 23:32.750
'Kay.

23:36.260 --> 23:37.310
<b>Next Time</b>

23:36.960 --> 23:39.640
Next time: "Big Sister Forever."

23:37.350 --> 23:37.520
<b>Episode 12</b>

23:37.640 --> 23:41.970
<b>Episode 12</b>

23:37.970 --> 23:41.970
<b>Big Sister Forever</b>
